# The chip-sized SHA-256 CORE — a faithful SHA-256 compression shrunk to fit the soft-core's 256-word
# on-board IMEM (nexys_soc_full.v). It keeps the REAL round function and message-schedule mathematics
# unchanged — the SHA-256 sigma0/sigma1 (ssig0/ssig1, using rotr + the LOGICAL word32Shr), Sigma0/Sigma1
# (bsig0/bsig1, three rotr's), ch/maj (word_and/word_not/xor), the wrapping Word32 + accumulator, the
# FIPS-180-4 round constants K, the standard IV, and a Seq of Word32 message schedule on the heap — and
# reduces only the COUNT of rounds/constants (8 rounds, 8 K-words, a 4-word schedule extension) so the whole
# program fits <= 256 words. So it exercises EVERY Word32 instruction the full-core encoder lowers — word32,
# intOfWord32 (unsigned Show), rotr, word32Shr, word_and, word_or, word_not, xor, wrapping +, and a
# Seq of Word32 build/index — on real silicon. The full 64-round production hash is
# benchmarks/programs/sha256/interp.lg (614 words, above the on-board IMEM).

## To ssig0 (x: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return rotr(x, 7) xor rotr(x, 18) xor word32Shr(x, 3).

## To ssig1 (x: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return rotr(x, 17) xor rotr(x, 19) xor word32Shr(x, 10).

## To bsig0 (x: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return rotr(x, 2) xor rotr(x, 13) xor rotr(x, 22).

## To bsig1 (x: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return rotr(x, 6) xor rotr(x, 11) xor rotr(x, 25).

## To ch (x: Word32) and (y: Word32) and (z: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return word_and(x, y) xor word_and(word_not(x), z).

## To maj (x: Word32) and (y: Word32) and (z: Word32) -> Word32:
    Return word_and(x, y) xor word_and(x, z) xor word_and(y, z).

## Main

Let mutable kk be a new Seq of Word32.
Push word32(1116352408) to kk.
Push word32(1899447441) to kk.
Push word32(3049323471) to kk.
Push word32(3921009573) to kk.
Push word32(961987163) to kk.
Push word32(1508970993) to kk.
Push word32(2453635748) to kk.
Push word32(2870763221) to kk.

Let mutable sched be a new Seq of Word32.
Push word32(2147483648) to sched.
Let mutable z be 0.
While z is less than 14:
    Push word32(0) to sched.
    Set z to z + 1.
Push word32(256) to sched.
Repeat for t from 16 to 19:
    Let s0 be ssig0(item (t - 14) of sched).
    Let s1 be ssig1(item (t - 1) of sched).
    Let nw be s1 + (item (t - 6) of sched) + s0 + (item (t - 15) of sched).
    Push nw to sched.

Let mutable a be word32(1779033703).
Let mutable b be word32(3144134277).
Let mutable c be word32(1013904242).
Let mutable d be word32(2773480762).
Let mutable e be word32(1359893119).
Let mutable f be word32(2600822924).
Let mutable g be word32(528734635).
Let mutable h be word32(1541459225).
Repeat for t from 0 to 7:
    Let t1 be h + bsig1(e) + ch(e, f, g) + (item (t + 1) of kk) + (item (t + 1) of sched).
    Let t2 be bsig0(a) + maj(a, b, c).
    Set h to g.
    Set g to f.
    Set f to e.
    Set e to d + t1.
    Set d to c.
    Set c to b.
    Set b to a.
    Set a to t1 + t2.
Show intOfWord32(a).
Show intOfWord32(b).
Show intOfWord32(c).
Show intOfWord32(d).
